---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@/lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Shibboleth Link" description="Privacy policy for Shibboleth Link">
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <article class="mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-5">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-2 text-gray-400">Shibboleth Link</p>
      </div>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The Short Version</h2>
        <p>
          Shibboleth Link uses your UIUC and Discord accounts to grant roles in a Discord server. Before you link, the page tells you whether that server will store an ongoing connection between those accounts.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell your information or use it for advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Information We Receive</h2>
        <p>When you link, we may receive:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Your UIUC NetID.</li>
          <li>Your UIUC affiliation, such as student or staff.</li>
          <li>Your Discord username and user ID.</li>
          <li>The Discord server where you are linking.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We use this information to decide which Discord roles you should receive and to give those roles to your Discord account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Confirm Only</h2>
        <p>
          In Confirm Only mode, Shibboleth Link uses your information for that linking attempt and does not keep a permanent connection between your UIUC and Discord accounts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your NetID is not shared with the Discord server owners. If the server has enabled administrative logging, its administrators may see your Discord account, UIUC affiliation, roles granted, and any role-grant error.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Link and Store</h2>
        <p>
          In Link and Store mode, Shibboleth Link keeps a server-specific connection between your UIUC and Discord accounts. This record includes your Discord user ID, NetID, UIUC affiliations, and the dates when the record was created and last updated.
        </p>
        <p>
          Verified Server administrators can use Shibboleth Link to look up or export these stored records. A server may begin storing links before it becomes verified, so older records may become available to its administrators if it is verified later.
        </p>
        <p>
          Changing the server back to Confirm Only does not automatically remove records that were already stored. Server administrators can delete all stored links for their server using the available server administration tools.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Server Verification</h2>
        <p>
          Discord server owners and administrators can verify that they are a current UIUC student or staff member. For this process, we store the verifier's Discord user ID, NetID, UIUC affiliations, administrative status, verification date, and expiration date.
        </p>
        <p>
          Active verification normally expires on August 1. Verification completed during the renewal period before August 1 remains active through the following August 1.
        </p>
        <p>
          An expired record is no longer used as active proof, but we may retain the record for verification history, abuse investigation, and operator review.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Who Can See Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
          <li>You can review the information shown during the linking process before submitting.</li>
          <li>Discord server administrators may see the information described above, depending on the server's selected mode, verification status, and logging settings.</li>
          <li>The Shibboleth Link operator can access service data when needed to operate, secure, troubleshoot, and moderate the service.</li>
          <li>Third-party infrastructure providers may process technical information needed to host and protect the service.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Temporary and Operational Records</h2>
        <p>
          We keep short-lived records needed to complete sign-in safely and prevent replay or account mix-ups. These records expire and are automatically cleaned up after a safety period.
        </p>
        <p>
          We also keep Discord server settings, role mappings, bans, and limited audit records needed to operate and moderate the service.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Safety and Audit Records</h2>
        <p>
          We may keep records of administrative actions such as lookups, exports, deletions, verification changes, and bans. These records help us detect abuse, investigate problems, and moderate the service. They may include the action taken, relevant account or server IDs, result counts, and the Discord user ID of the administrator who performed the action.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Service Providers</h2>
        <p>
          We use third-party providers such as Cloudflare for hosting, storage, routing, and abuse protection, and Discord to provide bot commands, roles, and server administration features. These providers may process technical information needed to deliver and secure Shibboleth Link.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a Discord server owner enables administrative logging, Shibboleth Link sends the logged information to a Discord channel selected by that server's administrators. Access to that channel is controlled by the Discord server's own permissions and settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel flex flex-col gap-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Questions</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this policy or how your information is handled, please use the <a href={siteConfig.contactUrl}>contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
